  "result": "Week of Oct 26 \u2013 Nov 1 is planned. Stop reason: `all_slots_resolved`.\n\n**AI \u2014 skipped.** The calendar already has a one-off AI talk that week: \"Frontier Models & Policy\" at Harvard Kennedy School, Wed Oct 28, 6:00 PM (non-recurring public lecture). The two recurring classes, 15.071 and MAS.665, correctly did *not* count, nor did the thesis writing block. No AI scout was launched.\n\n**Art \u2014 booked and confirmed.** *Opening: Threads of Light \u2014 Contemporary Textile Art*, Fri Oct 30, 6\u20138 PM, Museum of Fine Arts Boston. Free with registration, confirmation #1, ~20 min travel. Artist Mira Solano is tier 2 (established), venue tier 3; it beat the only other verified option, a tier-1 emerging artist's gallery opening that was also suggested-donation. The form was autonomy tier 1 \u2014 every required field came from the profile, the optional phone stayed blank, and both pre-checked marketing opt-ins (newsletter, sponsor data sharing) were turned off before submitting. Submitted once; the page returned a confirmation, so no resubmit. Calendar event `fx_2042013e9a`.\n\nWorth noting: the scout's third candidate, a Harvard Art Museums gallery talk, failed verification \u2014 its registration page is actually drop-in, and admission is $25 without a student ID, so the `registration_state: open` on the record was wrong. The verifier catching that is the mechanism working as intended.\n\nLocation was unambiguous (Boston all week, no travel days), and the Oct 27 evening block from the 15.071 Homework 4 deadline never came into play. Nothing is waiting on Nicolas \u2014 `pending` is empty.",
